  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3102.26 Protocol",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3102.26 \"Protocol\" means \"protocol\" as defined in the US EPA's proposed Model Open Market Trading Rule (60 FR 39668, August 3, 1995), namely, \"a replicable and workable method to estimate the mass of emissions reductions, or the amount of DERs needed for compliance, that meets USEPA's approval criteria.\"\n\nSource. #6441, EXEMPT, eff 1-21-97",
